<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equated to FOB Omaha Basis as of 3 pm CDT and compared to Monday's 3 pm close, fresh loins were 1.00-3.00 higher; butts 1.00-3.00 higher; skinned hams steady to 1.00 higher; bellies 12-14#'s steady, 14-16#'s steady to 1.00 higher; lean trimmings fully steady. Trading moderate, with moderate demand and light to moderate offerings. -- USDA</p>
<p>Note: 2 lds fresh boneless picnic traded @ $75.00.</p>
